1
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:10,760
Chapter 23 A splendid midsummer shorn over England, skies so pure, sun so radiant as

2
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:17,220
were then seen in long succession, seldom favor even singly, our wave-girt land.

3
00:00:17,319 --> 00:00:22,319
It was as if a band of Italian days had come from the south, like a flock of

4
00:00:22,321 --> 00:00:26,940
glorious passenger-birds, and lighted to rest them on the cliffs of Albion.

5
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:33,339
The hay was all got in, the fields round thornfield were green and shorn,

6
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:40,019
the roads white and baked, the trees were in their dark prime, hedge and wood,

7
00:00:40,739 --> 00:00:43,790
full-leaved and deeply tinted, contrasted well

8
00:00:43,792 --> 00:00:46,580
with the sunny hue of the cleared meadows between.

9
00:00:48,319 --> 00:00:53,599
On midsummer eve, Adele, weary with gathering wild strawberries in hay lane

10
00:00:53,601 --> 00:00:56,419
half the day, had gone to bed with the sun.

11
00:00:57,319 --> 00:01:01,559
I watched her drop of sleep, and when I left her, I sought the garden.

12
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:05,220
It was now the sweetest hour of the 24.

13
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:11,400
Day its fervid fires had wasted, and you fell cool on panting plain,

14
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,019
and scorched summit.

15
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:19,099
Where the sun had gone down in simple state, pure of the pomp of clouds,

16
00:01:19,980 --> 00:01:25,160
spread a solemn purple, burning with the light of red jewel and furnace flame at

17
00:01:25,161 --> 00:01:31,839
one point, on one hill peak, and extending high and wide, soft and still softer,

18
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:33,500
over half heaven.

19
00:01:34,639 --> 00:01:41,000
The east had its own charm or fine deep blue, and its own modest gem, a rising and

20
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:47,160
solitary star, soon it would boast the moon, but she was yet beneath the horizon.

21
00:01:48,339 --> 00:01:51,260
I walked a while on the pavement, but a subtle

22
00:01:51,262 --> 00:01:55,040
well-known scent that of a cigar stole from some window.

23
00:01:55,980 --> 00:02:03,980
I saw the library tortured.

24
00:02:04,819 --> 00:02:08,500
No nook in the grounds more sheltered and more Eden-like.

25
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:10,220
It was full of trees.

26
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:11,540
It bloomed with flowers.

27
00:02:12,379 --> 00:02:17,139
A very high wall shot it out from the court, on one side, on the other,

28
00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:19,720
a beach avenue screened it from the lawn.

29
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:23,300
At the bottom was a sunk fence.

30
00:02:24,319 --> 00:02:29,135
It's sole separation from lonely fields, a winding walk,

31
00:02:29,137 --> 00:02:32,879
bordered with laurels and terminating in a giant horse chestnut.

32
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:36,699
Circled at the base by a seat, led down to the fence.

33
00:02:37,639 --> 00:02:40,099
Here one could wander unseen.

34
00:02:41,239 --> 00:02:46,940
While such honeydew fell, such silence reigned, such gloaming gathered,

35
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:50,360
I felt as if I could haunt such shade forever.

36
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:54,860
But in threading the flower and fruit partairs, at the upper part of the

37
00:02:54,860 --> 00:02:58,446
enclosure, enticed there, by the light the now

38
00:02:58,447 --> 00:03:01,440
rising moon, cast on this more open quarter.

39
00:03:02,019 --> 00:03:08,760
My step is stayed, not by sound, not by sight, but once more by a warning fragrance.

40
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:14,500
Sweet briar and southern wood, jasmine, pink and rose have long been

41
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:16,800
yielding their evening sacrifice of incense.

42
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:20,900
This new scent is neither of shrub nor flower.

43
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:23,059
It is, I know it well.

44
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:25,300
It is Mr. Rochester's cigar.

45
00:03:26,239 --> 00:03:27,879
I look round and I listen.

46
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:31,260
I see trees laden with ripening fruit.

47
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:35,019
I hear a nightingale warbling in a wood half a mile off.

48
00:03:35,459 --> 00:03:36,980
No moving form is visible.

49
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:38,940
No coming step audible.

50
00:03:39,660 --> 00:03:41,059
But that perfume increases.

51
00:03:41,919 --> 00:03:42,919
I must flee.

52
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:47,103
I make for the wicked leading to the shrubbery, and I see Mr.

53
00:03:47,103 --> 00:03:48,720
Rochester entering.

54
00:03:49,199 --> 00:03:51,360
I step aside into the ivy recess.

55
00:03:52,379 --> 00:03:53,540
He will not stay long.

56
00:03:54,279 --> 00:03:56,099
He will soon return once he came.

57
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:59,459
And if I sit still he will never see me.

58
00:04:00,099 --> 00:04:01,099
But no.

59
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:07,400
Even tide is as pleasant to him as to me, and this antique garden as attractive.

60
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:13,279
And he strolls on, now lifting the gooseberry tree branches to look at the

61
00:04:13,281 --> 00:04:16,580
fruit, largest plums with which they are laden.

62
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:22,760
Now taking a ripe cherry from the wall, now stooping towards a knot of flowers,

63
00:04:23,580 --> 00:04:28,220
either to inhale their fragrance or to admire the dewbeats on their petals.

64
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:32,000
A great moth goes humming by me.

65
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:35,400
It elites on a plant at Mr. Rochester's foot.

66
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:38,819
He sees it, and bends to examine it.

67
00:04:40,459 --> 00:04:45,879
Now he has his back towards me, thought I, and he has occupied too.

68
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:49,819
Perhaps if I walk softly I can slip away unnoticed.

69
00:04:50,639 --> 00:04:53,167
I trod on an edging of turf that the crackle

70
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:56,120
of the pebbly gravel might not betray me.

71
00:04:56,620 --> 00:05:01,779
He was standing among the beds at a yard or two distant from where I had to pass.

72
00:05:02,620 --> 00:05:04,940
The moth apparently engaged him.

73
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:08,900
I shall get by very well, I meditated.

74
00:05:10,239 --> 00:05:15,059
As I crossed his shadow thrown long over the garden by the moon, not yet risen high.

75
00:05:15,779 --> 00:05:17,580
He said quietly, without turning.

76
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:20,940
Jane, come and look at this fellow.

77
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,139
I had made no noise.

78
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,239
He had not eyes behind.

79
00:05:25,879 --> 00:05:26,879
Could his shadow feel?

80
00:05:27,959 --> 00:05:30,660
I started at first, and then I approached him.

81
00:05:31,739 --> 00:05:33,819
Look at his wings," said he.

82
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:37,099
He reminds me rather of a West Indian insect.

83
00:05:38,019 --> 00:05:40,860
One does not often see so large and gay a night rover in England.

84
00:05:41,339 --> 00:05:43,279
There, he is flown.

85
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:45,680
The moth roamed away.

86
00:05:46,660 --> 00:05:51,099
I was sheepishly retreating also, but Mr. Rochester followed me.

87
00:05:51,860 --> 00:05:55,800
And when we reached the wicked, he said, turn back.

88
00:05:56,419 --> 00:06:02,559
On so lovely a night it is a shame to sit in the house, and surely no one can wish

89
00:06:02,561 --> 00:06:06,639
to go to bed while sunset is thus at meeting with moonrise.

90
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:13,220
It is one of my faults, that though my tongue is sometimes prompt enough at an

91
00:06:13,220 --> 00:06:17,919
answer, there are times when it sadly fails me in framing and excuse.

92
00:06:19,099 --> 00:06:25,959
And always, the laps occurs at some crisis when a facile word or plausible pretext is

93
00:06:25,961 --> 00:06:29,220
specially wanted to get me out of painful embarrassment.

94
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:36,480
I did not like to walk at this hour alone with Mr. Rochester in the shadowy orchard.

95
00:06:37,410 --> 00:06:40,739
But I could not find a reason to allege for leaving him.

96
00:06:42,019 --> 00:06:46,072
I followed with lagging step, and thoughts busily

97
00:06:46,074 --> 00:06:49,561
bent on discovering a means of extrication.

98
00:06:50,699 --> 00:06:54,099
But he himself looked so composed and so grave also.

99
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:57,400
I became ashamed of feeling any confusion.

100
00:06:58,300 --> 00:07:04,290
The evil, if evil existent or expected there was, seemed to lie with me only.

101
00:07:05,110 --> 00:07:06,949
His mind was unconscious and quiet.

102
00:07:08,029 --> 00:07:14,750
Jane, he recommenced, as we entered the laurel walk, and slowly strayed down in

103
00:07:14,750 --> 00:07:17,349
the direction of the sunk fence and the horse chestnut.

104
00:07:18,370 --> 00:07:21,169
Thornfield is a pleasant place in summer, is it not?

105
00:07:22,589 --> 00:07:23,589
Yes, sir.

106
00:07:24,510 --> 00:07:27,330
You must have become in some degree attached to the house.

107
00:07:28,230 --> 00:07:31,584
You, who have an eye for natural beauties,

108
00:07:31,586 --> 00:07:35,031
and a good deal of the organ of adhesiveness.

109
00:07:36,010 --> 00:07:37,529
I am attached to it indeed.

110
00:07:38,569 --> 00:07:43,230
And though I don't comprehend how it is, I perceive you have acquired a degree of

111
00:07:43,230 --> 00:07:45,709
regard for that foolish little child, Adele, too.

112
00:07:46,510 --> 00:07:48,709
And even for simple dame fair facts?

113
00:07:49,930 --> 00:07:50,930
Yes, sir.

114
00:07:51,209 --> 00:07:54,069
In different ways, I have an affection for both.

115
00:07:54,790 --> 00:07:56,589
And would be sorry to part with them.

116
00:07:57,330 --> 00:08:01,650
Yes, pity, he said, and sighed and paused.

117
00:08:02,389 --> 00:08:05,589
It is always the way of events in this life.

118
00:08:06,349 --> 00:08:07,769
He continued presently.

119
00:08:08,690 --> 00:08:12,029
No sooner have you got settled in a pleasant resting

120
00:08:12,031 --> 00:08:15,730
place than a voice calls out to you to rise and move on.

121
00:08:16,330 --> 00:08:18,349
For the hour of repose is expired.

122
00:08:19,830 --> 00:08:21,110
Must I move on, sir?

123
00:08:21,569 --> 00:08:21,949
I asked.

124
00:08:22,510 --> 00:08:23,669
Must I leave Thornfield?

125
00:08:24,389 --> 00:08:25,870
I believe you must, Jane.

126
00:08:26,250 --> 00:08:27,269
I am sorry, Janet.

127
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:29,510
But I believe indeed you must.

128
00:08:30,269 --> 00:08:31,269
This was a blow.

129
00:08:31,949 --> 00:08:34,010
But I did not let it frustrate me.

130
00:08:35,730 --> 00:08:38,910
Well, sir, I shall be ready when the order to march comes.

131
00:08:39,970 --> 00:08:41,029
It is come now.

132
00:08:41,190 --> 00:08:42,190
I must give it to night.

133
00:08:43,349 --> 00:08:45,410
Then you are going to be married, sir.

134
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:49,709
Exactly, precisely, with your usual acuteness,

135
00:08:49,711 --> 00:08:52,571
you have hit the nail straight on the head.

136
00:08:53,290 --> 00:08:55,970
Soon, sir, very soon, my.

137
00:08:57,050 --> 00:08:58,230
That is, miss air.

138
00:08:59,150 --> 00:09:04,510
And you'll remember, Jane, the first time I or rumor plainly intimated to you that

139
00:09:04,510 --> 00:09:09,349
it was my intention to put my old bachelor's neck into the sacred noose,

140
00:09:10,169 --> 00:09:13,205
to enter into the holiest state of matrimony,

141
00:09:13,205 --> 00:09:16,510
to take Miss Ingram to my bosom in short.

142
00:09:16,970 --> 00:09:20,410
She's an extensive armful, but that's not to the point.

143
00:09:21,309 --> 00:09:25,650
One can't have too much of such a very excellent thing as my beautiful blanche.

144
00:09:26,529 --> 00:09:30,230
Well, as I was saying, listen to me, Jane.

145
00:09:31,209 --> 00:09:33,989
You're not turning your head to look after more moths, are you?

146
00:09:34,529 --> 00:09:38,190
That was only a lady-clock child, flying away home.

147
00:09:39,349 --> 00:09:42,857
I wish to remind you that it was you who first

148
00:09:42,858 --> 00:09:46,290
said to me with that discretion I respect in you.

149
00:09:46,730 --> 00:09:53,010
With that foresight, prudence, and humility which befit your responsible

150
00:09:53,010 --> 00:09:58,146
and dependent position, that in case I married Miss Ingram,

151
00:09:58,148 --> 00:10:02,069
both you and little Adele had better trot forthwith.

152
00:10:02,970 --> 00:10:05,567
I pass over the sort of slur conveyed in this

153
00:10:05,567 --> 00:10:08,790
suggestion on the character of my beloved.

154
00:10:09,010 --> 00:10:13,989
Indeed, when you are far away, Janet, I'll try to forget it.

155
00:10:14,589 --> 00:10:20,391
I shall notice only its wisdom, which is such that I have made it my law of action.

156
00:10:21,230 --> 00:10:25,589
Adele must go to school, and you, Miss Air, must get a new situation.

157
00:10:26,650 --> 00:10:27,650
Yes, sir.

158
00:10:27,849 --> 00:10:29,290
I will advertise immediately.

159
00:10:30,089 --> 00:10:32,050
And, mean time, I suppose.

160
00:10:33,370 --> 00:10:36,883
I was going to say, I suppose I may stay here,

161
00:10:36,883 --> 00:10:40,391
till I find another shelter to but take myself to.

162
00:10:41,430 --> 00:10:45,667
But I stopped, feeling it would not do to risk a long

163
00:10:45,669 --> 00:10:49,370
sentence, for my voice was not quite under command.

164
00:10:51,269 --> 00:10:56,250
In about a month, I hoped to be a bridegroom, continued Mr. Rochester,

165
00:10:57,169 --> 00:11:02,669
and in the interim, I shall myself look out for employment and an asylum for you.

166
00:11:04,069 --> 00:11:05,230
Thank you, sir.

167
00:11:05,870 --> 00:11:11,269
I am sorry to give, oh, no need to apologize, I consider that when a

168
00:11:11,271 --> 00:11:16,830
dependent does her duty as well as you have done yours, she has a sort of claim

169
00:11:16,830 --> 00:11:21,410
upon her employer for any little assistance he can conveniently render her.

170
00:11:23,089 --> 00:11:26,578
Indeed, I have already, through my future

171
00:11:26,578 --> 00:11:30,709
mother-in-law, heard of a place that I think will suit.

172
00:11:31,790 --> 00:11:36,411
It is to undertake the education of the five daughters of Mrs.

173
00:11:36,891 --> 00:11:40,550
Dionysius, a gal of Biddonut Lodge, Conort Island.

174
00:11:42,129 --> 00:11:43,690
You'll like Island, I think.

175
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:46,290
They're such warm-hearted people there, they say.

176
00:11:47,309 --> 00:11:48,389
It is a long way off, sir.

177
00:11:49,709 --> 00:11:54,110
No matter, the girl of your sense will not object to the voyage or the distance.

178
00:11:55,089 --> 00:12:00,190
Not the voyage, but the distance and then the sea is a barrier.

179
00:12:01,910 --> 00:12:02,910
From what, Jane?

180
00:12:03,830 --> 00:12:09,730
From England and from Thornfield and, well, from you, sir.

181
00:12:10,949 --> 00:12:14,425
I said this almost involuntarily, and with this

182
00:12:14,427 --> 00:12:18,970
little sanction of free will, my tears gushed out.

183
00:12:19,730 --> 00:12:24,050
I did not cry so as to be heard, however, I avoided sobbing.

184
00:12:25,129 --> 00:12:30,169
The thought of Mrs. O'Gall and Biddonut Lodge struck cold to my heart,

185
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:36,029
and colder the thought of all the brine and foam, destined as it seemed to rush

186
00:12:36,031 --> 00:12:41,809
between me and the master at whose side I now walked, and called us the remembrance

187
00:12:41,811 --> 00:12:47,650
of the wider ocean, wealth, caste, custom, intervened between me,

188
00:12:48,230 --> 00:12:51,190
and what I naturally and inevitably loved.

189
00:12:52,589 --> 00:12:55,269
It is a long way, I again said.

190
00:12:55,970 --> 00:13:01,629
It is to be sure, and when you get to Biddonut Lodge, Conort Island,

191
00:13:02,330 --> 00:13:04,029
I shall never see you again, Jane.

192
00:13:04,529 --> 00:13:05,610
That's morally certain.

193
00:13:06,330 --> 00:13:10,629
I never go over to Ireland, not having myself much of a fancy for the country.

194
00:13:12,290 --> 00:13:14,010
We have been good friends, Jane.

195
00:13:15,110 --> 00:13:16,110
Have we not?

196
00:13:16,949 --> 00:13:17,949
Yes, sir.

197
00:13:18,750 --> 00:13:23,569
And when friends are on the eve of separation, they like to spend the little

198
00:13:23,571 --> 00:13:26,529
time that remains to them, close to each other.

199
00:13:28,150 --> 00:13:33,089
Come, we'll talk over the voyage and the parting, quietly half an hour or so,

200
00:13:33,910 --> 00:13:37,430
while the stars enter into their shining life up in heaven yonder.

201
00:13:38,370 --> 00:13:39,529
Here is the chestnut tree.

202
00:13:40,510 --> 00:13:42,330
Here is the bench at its old roots.

203
00:13:43,410 --> 00:13:46,785
Come, we will sit there in peace tonight, though we

204
00:13:46,786 --> 00:13:49,790
should never more be destined to sit there together.

205
00:13:50,489 --> 00:13:52,290
He seated me and himself.

206
00:13:53,290 --> 00:13:56,129
It is a long way to Ireland, Janet, and I am sorry

207
00:13:56,129 --> 00:13:58,809
to send my little friend on such weary travels.

208
00:13:59,589 --> 00:14:02,290
But if I can't do better, how is it to be helped?

209
00:14:03,129 --> 00:14:05,190
Are you anything akin to me, do you think, Jane?

210
00:14:06,949 --> 00:14:09,650
I could risk no sort of answer by this time.

211
00:14:10,330 --> 00:14:11,589
My heart was still.

212
00:14:13,349 --> 00:14:17,555
Because, he said, I sometimes have a queer feeling with

213
00:14:17,555 --> 00:14:22,290
regard to you, especially when you are near me, as now.

214
00:14:23,309 --> 00:14:29,589
It is as if I had a string somewhere under my left ribs tightly and inextricably

215
00:14:29,591 --> 00:14:32,055
knotted to a similar string situated in the

216
00:14:32,057 --> 00:14:35,571
corresponding quarter of your little frame.

217
00:14:35,730 --> 00:14:41,370
And if that boisterous channel and 200 miles or so of land come broad between us,

218
00:14:41,949 --> 00:14:45,610
I am afraid that cord of communion will be snapped.

219
00:14:46,349 --> 00:14:52,230
And then, I have a nervous notion I should take to bleeding inwardly, as for you,

220
00:14:52,690 --> 00:14:53,690
you'd forget me.

221
00:14:55,089 --> 00:14:56,550
That I never should, sir.

222
00:14:57,410 --> 00:14:59,290
You know, impossible to proceed.

223
00:15:00,449 --> 00:15:03,169
Jane, do you hear that nightingale singing in the wood?

224
00:15:03,889 --> 00:15:08,589
Listen, in listening, I sobbed convulsively.

225
00:15:09,290 --> 00:15:11,410
For I could repress what I endured no longer.

226
00:15:12,010 --> 00:15:13,190
I was obliged to yield.

227
00:15:13,949 --> 00:15:16,529
And I was shaken from head to foot with acute distress.

228
00:15:17,529 --> 00:15:21,733
When I did speak, it was only to express an impetuous wish

229
00:15:21,733 --> 00:15:25,669
that I had never been born or never come to thornfield.

230
00:15:26,790 --> 00:15:28,669
Because you are sorry to leave it?

231
00:15:30,110 --> 00:15:35,129
The vehement of emotion stirred by grief and love within me was claiming mastery

232
00:15:35,131 --> 00:15:38,069
and struggling for full sway and asserting a right to

233
00:15:38,069 --> 00:15:41,690
predominate to overcome to live, rise, and reign at last.

234
00:15:42,529 --> 00:15:44,489
Yes, and to speak.

235
00:15:46,129 --> 00:15:47,849
I grieve to leave thornfield.

236
00:15:48,690 --> 00:15:50,050
I love thornfield.

237
00:15:50,809 --> 00:15:51,809
I love it.

238
00:15:52,150 --> 00:15:57,370
Because I have lived in it a full and delightful life, momentarily at least.

239
00:15:57,889 --> 00:15:59,290
I have not been trampled on.

240
00:15:59,930 --> 00:16:01,489
I have not been petrified.

241
00:16:02,010 --> 00:16:07,069
I have not been buried with inferior minds, and excluded from every glimpse of

242
00:16:07,071 --> 00:16:10,970
communion with what is bright and energetic and high.

243
00:16:12,150 --> 00:16:17,750
I have talked face to face with what I reverence, with what I delight in,

244
00:16:18,150 --> 00:16:21,830
with an original, a vigorous and expanded mind.

245
00:16:22,669 --> 00:16:24,970
I have known you, Mr. Rochester.

246
00:16:25,690 --> 00:16:28,021
And it strikes me with terror and anguish to

247
00:16:28,023 --> 00:16:31,491
feel I absolutely must be torn from you forever.

248
00:16:31,750 --> 00:16:38,050
I see the necessity of departure, and it is like looking on the necessity of death.

249
00:16:38,889 --> 00:16:40,510
Where do you see the necessity?

250
00:16:41,309 --> 00:16:42,309
He asked suddenly.

251
00:16:43,089 --> 00:16:43,370
Where?

252
00:16:43,889 --> 00:16:45,349
You sir, have placed it before me.

253
00:16:46,069 --> 00:16:47,069
In what shape?

254
00:16:47,110 --> 00:16:51,449
In the shape of Miss Ingram, a noble and beautiful woman, your bride.

255
00:16:52,129 --> 00:16:53,129
My bride.

256
00:16:53,370 --> 00:16:54,370
What bride?

257
00:16:54,569 --> 00:16:55,569
I have no bride.

258
00:16:56,029 --> 00:16:57,110
But you will have.

259
00:16:57,870 --> 00:16:59,029
Yes, I will.

260
00:16:59,470 --> 00:17:00,069
I will.

261
00:17:00,309 --> 00:17:01,529
He set his teeth.

262
00:17:02,430 --> 00:17:03,430
Then I must go.

263
00:17:03,569 --> 00:17:04,610
You have said it yourself.

264
00:17:05,110 --> 00:17:07,129
No, you must stay.

265
00:17:07,550 --> 00:17:10,050
I swear it, and the oath shall be kept.

266
00:17:11,389 --> 00:17:12,449
I tell you, I must go.

267
00:17:13,089 --> 00:17:16,069
I retorted, roused to something like passion.

268
00:17:17,110 --> 00:17:19,150
Do you think I can stay to become nothing to you?

269
00:17:20,069 --> 00:17:21,309
Do you think I am an automaton?

270
00:17:22,129 --> 00:17:27,669
A machine without feelings, and compare to have my morsel of bread snatched from my

271
00:17:27,671 --> 00:17:31,269
lips, and my drop of living water dashed from my cup.

272
00:17:32,529 --> 00:17:35,286
Do you think, because I am poor, obscure,

273
00:17:35,288 --> 00:17:38,330
plain, and little, I am solace and heartless?

274
00:17:38,709 --> 00:17:39,709
You think wrong.

275
00:17:40,470 --> 00:17:46,629
I have as much soul as you, and full as much heart, and if God had gifted me with

276
00:17:46,631 --> 00:17:51,529
some beauty and much wealth, I should have made it as hard for you to leave me,

277
00:17:52,290 --> 00:17:54,849
as it is now for me to leave you.

278
00:17:55,809 --> 00:18:00,550
I am not talking to you now through the medium of custom, conventionalities,

279
00:18:00,809 --> 00:18:02,730
nor even of mortal flesh.

280
00:18:03,389 --> 00:18:10,150
It is my spirit that addresses your spirit, just as if both had passed through

281
00:18:10,150 --> 00:18:14,889
the grave, and we stood at God's feet equal as we are.

282
00:18:16,169 --> 00:18:23,589
As we are, repeated Mr. Rochester, so he added, enclosing me in his arms,

283
00:18:24,110 --> 00:18:27,470
gathering me to his breast, pressing his lips on my lips.

284
00:18:28,470 --> 00:18:29,650
So, Jane.

285
00:18:32,349 --> 00:18:40,349
Yes, so, sir, I rejoined, and yet not so, for you are a married man, or as good as a

286
00:18:40,351 --> 00:18:45,069
married man, and wed to one inferior to you, to one with whom you have no

287
00:18:45,071 --> 00:18:51,050
sympathy, whom I do not believe you truly love, for I have seen and heard you sneer

288
00:18:51,050 --> 00:18:56,510
at her, I would scorn such a union, therefore I am better than you, let me go.

289
00:18:57,250 --> 00:18:58,610
Where, Jane, to Ireland?

290
00:18:59,470 --> 00:19:01,569
Yes, to Ireland.

291
00:19:02,290 --> 00:19:05,550
I have spoken my mind and can go anywhere now.

292
00:19:06,709 --> 00:19:08,010
Jane, be still.

293
00:19:08,750 --> 00:19:11,366
Don't struggle so, like a wild frantic bird that

294
00:19:11,366 --> 00:19:14,010
is rending its own plumage in its desperation.

295
00:19:15,370 --> 00:19:18,550
I am no bird, and no net and snares me.

296
00:19:19,209 --> 00:19:24,811
I am a free human being with an independent will, which I now exert to leave you.

297
00:19:25,769 --> 00:19:31,989
Another effort set me at liberty, and I stood erect before him, and your

298
00:19:31,991 --> 00:19:34,470
will shall decide your destiny, he said.

299
00:19:35,250 --> 00:19:39,870
I offer you my hand, my heart, and a share of all my possessions.

300
00:19:40,870 --> 00:19:43,730
You play a force, which I merely laugh at.

301
00:19:44,410 --> 00:19:48,116
I ask you to pass through life at my side, to

302
00:19:48,118 --> 00:19:52,091
be my second self, and best earthly companion.

303
00:19:52,669 --> 00:19:56,489
For that fate you have already made your choice and must abide by it.

304
00:19:57,449 --> 00:20:03,110
Jane, be still a few moments, you are overexcited, I will be still too.

305
00:20:04,790 --> 00:20:09,809
A woft of wind came sweeping down the loral walk, and trembled through the

306
00:20:09,811 --> 00:20:17,669
boughs of the chestnut, it wandered away, away, to an indefinite distance, it died.

307
00:20:18,069 --> 00:20:22,889
The nightingale's song was then the only voice of the hour, in listening to it,

308
00:20:23,250 --> 00:20:24,470
I again wept.

309
00:20:25,510 --> 00:20:29,510
Mr. Rochester sat quiet, looking at me gently and seriously.

310
00:20:30,690 --> 00:20:34,410
Some time passed before he spoke, he at last said.

311
00:20:35,290 --> 00:20:39,970
Come to my side, Jane, and let us explain and understand one another.

312
00:20:41,230 --> 00:20:46,330
I will never again come to your side, I am torn away now and cannot return.

313
00:20:47,449 --> 00:20:52,050
But Jane, I summon you as my wife, it is you only I intend to marry.

314
00:20:52,989 --> 00:20:55,529
I was silent, I thought he mocked me.

315
00:20:56,389 --> 00:20:57,529
Come Jane, come hither.

316
00:20:58,230 --> 00:20:59,949
Your bride stands between us.

317
00:21:00,870 --> 00:21:02,870
He rose, and with a stride reached me.

318
00:21:03,930 --> 00:21:06,896
My bride is here, he said, again drawing me to

319
00:21:06,896 --> 00:21:10,470
him, because my equal is here and my likeness.

320
00:21:10,809 --> 00:21:12,730
Jane, will you marry me?

321
00:21:14,089 --> 00:21:18,709
Still, I did not answer, and still I writhed myself from his grasp,

322
00:21:19,430 --> 00:21:20,569
for I was still incredulous.

323
00:21:21,449 --> 00:21:22,449
Do you doubt me, Jane?

324
00:21:23,669 --> 00:21:26,449
Entirely, you have no faith in me.

325
00:21:27,029 --> 00:21:28,029
Not a wit.

326
00:21:29,089 --> 00:21:30,650
Am I a liar in your eyes?

327
00:21:31,370 --> 00:21:32,370
He asked passionately.

328
00:21:33,269 --> 00:21:34,970
Little skeptic, you should be convinced.

329
00:21:35,790 --> 00:21:37,129
What love have I for Miss Ingram?

330
00:21:37,750 --> 00:21:37,870
None.

331
00:21:38,470 --> 00:21:41,610
And that you know, what love has she for me?

332
00:21:42,129 --> 00:21:43,129
None.

333
00:21:43,290 --> 00:21:48,250
As I have taken pains to prove, I caused a rumour to reach her that my

334
00:21:48,250 --> 00:21:50,730
fortune was not a third of what was supposed.

335
00:21:51,690 --> 00:21:54,949
And after that, I presented myself to see the result.

336
00:21:55,730 --> 00:21:58,750
It was coldness, both from her and her mother.

337
00:21:59,550 --> 00:22:00,550
I would not.

338
00:22:00,709 --> 00:22:03,110
I could not marry Miss Ingram.

339
00:22:03,989 --> 00:22:06,610
You, you strange, you almost unearthly thing.

340
00:22:07,209 --> 00:22:08,309
I love as my own flesh.

341
00:22:09,010 --> 00:22:12,129
You, poor and obscure, and small and plain as you are.

342
00:22:12,949 --> 00:22:14,529
I entreated to accept me as a husband.

343
00:22:15,430 --> 00:22:15,790
What?

344
00:22:16,209 --> 00:22:16,410
Me?

345
00:22:17,190 --> 00:22:20,260
I ejaculated, beginning in his earnestness, and

346
00:22:20,260 --> 00:22:23,430
especially in his incivility, to credit his sincerity.

347
00:22:24,730 --> 00:22:28,610
Me who have not a friend in the world, but you, if you are my friend,

348
00:22:29,110 --> 00:22:31,589
not a shilling, but what you have given me.

349
00:22:32,629 --> 00:22:36,769
You, Jane, I must have you for my own entirely my own.

350
00:22:37,790 --> 00:22:38,790
Will you be mine?

351
00:22:38,870 --> 00:22:39,889
Say yes, quickly.

352
00:22:41,050 --> 00:22:43,470
Mr. Rochester, let me look at your face.

353
00:22:44,349 --> 00:22:45,349
Turn to the moonlight.

354
00:22:46,230 --> 00:22:47,230
Why?

355
00:22:47,529 --> 00:22:49,349
Because I want to read your countenance.

356
00:22:49,669 --> 00:22:50,669
Turn.

357
00:22:50,910 --> 00:22:51,910
There.

358
00:22:52,269 --> 00:22:57,309
You will find it scarcely more legible than a crumpled scratched page.

359
00:22:57,830 --> 00:22:58,290
Read on.

360
00:22:58,730 --> 00:23:00,589
Only make haste for ice suffer.

361
00:23:01,690 --> 00:23:06,489
His face was very much agitated and very much flushed, and there were strong

362
00:23:06,491 --> 00:23:10,389
workings in the features and strange gleams in the eyes.

363
00:23:11,250 --> 00:23:13,489
Oh, Jane, you torture me.

364
00:23:14,230 --> 00:23:15,230
He exclaimed.

365
00:23:15,730 --> 00:23:20,370
With that searching and yet faithful and generous look, you torture me.

366
00:23:21,870 --> 00:23:25,949
How can I do that if you are true and you offer real?

367
00:23:26,750 --> 00:23:29,650
My only feelings to you must be gratitude and devotion.

368
00:23:30,309 --> 00:23:31,309
They cannot torture.

369
00:23:32,410 --> 00:23:33,410
Gratitude?

370
00:23:33,650 --> 00:23:36,250
He ejaculated and added wildly.

371
00:23:37,089 --> 00:23:38,269
Jane accept me quickly.

372
00:23:38,669 --> 00:23:40,069
Say, Edward, give me my name.

373
00:23:40,470 --> 00:23:42,050
Edward, I will marry you.

374
00:23:43,129 --> 00:23:44,169
Are you an earnest?

375
00:23:45,110 --> 00:23:46,169
Do you truly love me?

376
00:23:47,069 --> 00:23:48,910
Do you sincerely wish me to be your wife?

377
00:23:50,389 --> 00:23:51,389
I do.

378
00:23:51,730 --> 00:23:54,910
And if an oath is necessary to satisfy you, I swear it.

379
00:23:55,809 --> 00:23:57,589
Then, sir, I will marry you.

380
00:23:58,529 --> 00:24:00,250
Edward, my little wife.

381
00:24:00,870 --> 00:24:02,870
Dear Edward, come to me.

382
00:24:03,349 --> 00:24:07,690
Come to me entirely now, said he, and added in his deepest tone,

383
00:24:08,029 --> 00:24:10,569
speaking in my ear as his cheek was laid on mine.

384
00:24:11,550 --> 00:24:12,970
Make my happiness.

385
00:24:13,550 --> 00:24:15,029
I will make yours.

386
00:24:16,010 --> 00:24:20,370
God pardon me, he subjoined air-long, and man medall not with me.

387
00:24:21,029 --> 00:24:23,110
I have her, and will hold her.

388
00:24:24,250 --> 00:24:25,750
There is no one to medall, sir.

389
00:24:26,430 --> 00:24:28,089
I have no kindred to interfere.

390
00:24:30,330 --> 00:24:33,470
No, that is the best of it, he said.

391
00:24:34,290 --> 00:24:37,578
And if I had loved him less, I should have thought

392
00:24:37,578 --> 00:24:40,370
his accent and look of exaltation's savage.

393
00:24:41,250 --> 00:24:46,769
But, sitting by him, roused from the nightmare of parting, called to the

394
00:24:46,771 --> 00:24:49,252
paradise of union, I thought only of the

395
00:24:49,254 --> 00:24:53,290
bliss given me to drink in so abundant a flow.

396
00:24:53,430 --> 00:24:58,910
Again and again, he said, are you happy, Jane, and again and again I answered,

397
00:24:59,389 --> 00:25:05,309
yes, after which he murmured, it will atone, it will atone.

398
00:25:06,250 --> 00:25:09,629
Have I not found her friendless and cold and comfortless?

399
00:25:10,750 --> 00:25:13,629
Will I not guard and cherish and solace her?

400
00:25:14,910 --> 00:25:18,970
Is there not love in my heart and constancy in my resolves?

401
00:25:19,769 --> 00:25:21,610
It will expiate at God's tribunal.

402
00:25:22,849 --> 00:25:24,970
I know my maker's sanctions what I do.

403
00:25:25,669 --> 00:25:28,449
For the world's judgment, I wash my hands thereof.

404
00:25:29,209 --> 00:25:31,370
For man's opinion, I defy it.

405
00:25:32,290 --> 00:25:33,910
But what had before in the night?

406
00:25:34,949 --> 00:25:38,230
The moon was not yet set, and we were all in shadow.

407
00:25:38,610 --> 00:25:41,849
I could scarcely see my master's face near as I was.

408
00:25:43,150 --> 00:25:47,605
And what ailed the chestnut tree it writhed and groaned,

409
00:25:47,607 --> 00:25:51,290
while wind roared in the loral walk and came sweeping over us.

410
00:25:52,470 --> 00:25:56,709
We must go in, said Mr. Rochester, the weather changes.

411
00:25:57,849 --> 00:25:59,930
I could have sat with thee till morning, Jane.

412
00:26:01,029 --> 00:26:04,529
And so thought I, could I with you.

413
00:26:05,750 --> 00:26:10,165
I should have said so perhaps, but a livid, vivid

414
00:26:10,167 --> 00:26:12,889
spark leapt out of a cloud at which I was looking.

415
00:26:13,449 --> 00:26:17,830
And there was a crack, a crash, and a close rattling peel.

416
00:26:18,790 --> 00:26:22,809
And I thought only of hiding my dazzled eyes against Mr. Rochester's shoulder.

417
00:26:23,949 --> 00:26:25,510
The rain rushed down.

418
00:26:26,290 --> 00:26:30,610
He hurried me up the walk, through the grounds, and into the house.

419
00:26:31,269 --> 00:26:34,709
But we were quite wet before we could pass the threshold.

420
00:26:35,610 --> 00:26:40,349
He was taking off my shawl in the hall, and shaking the water out of my loosened

421
00:26:40,351 --> 00:26:43,910
hair, when Mrs. Fairfax emerged from her room.

422
00:26:45,069 --> 00:26:48,949
I did not observe her at first, nor did Mr. Rochester.

423
00:26:50,250 --> 00:26:51,250
The lamp was lit.

424
00:26:52,029 --> 00:26:54,209
The clock was on the stroke of twelve.

425
00:26:56,150 --> 00:26:59,190
Haste and to take off your wet things, said he.

426
00:26:59,809 --> 00:27:01,010
And before you go, good night.

427
00:27:01,849 --> 00:27:02,849
Good night, my darling.

428
00:27:03,650 --> 00:27:04,750
He kissed me repeatedly.

429
00:27:05,849 --> 00:27:11,849
When I looked up, on leaving his arms, there stood the widow, pale, grave,

430
00:27:12,370 --> 00:27:13,370
and amazed.

431
00:27:13,750 --> 00:27:16,290
I only smiled at her, and ran upstairs.

432
00:27:17,629 --> 00:27:20,629
Explanation will do for another time, thought I.

433
00:27:21,449 --> 00:27:25,669
Still, when I reached my chamber, I felt a pang at the idea

434
00:27:25,669 --> 00:27:29,489
she should even temporarily misconstrue what she had seen.

435
00:27:30,529 --> 00:27:37,610
But joy soon effaced every other feeling, and loud as the wind blew, near and deep

436
00:27:37,610 --> 00:27:42,389
as the thunder crashed, fierce and frequent as the lightning gleamed,

437
00:27:42,830 --> 00:27:46,750
cataract-like as the rain fell during a storm of two hours' duration.

438
00:27:47,750 --> 00:27:50,569
I experienced no fear and little awe.

439
00:27:51,970 --> 00:27:57,610
Mr. Rochester came thrice to my door in the course of it, to ask if I was safe and

440
00:27:57,610 --> 00:28:02,650
tranquil, and that was comfort, that was strength for anything.

441
00:28:03,830 --> 00:28:08,709
Before I left my bed in the morning, little Adele came running in to tell me

442
00:28:08,711 --> 00:28:13,550
that the great horse chestnut at the bottom of the orchard had been struck by

443
00:28:13,550 --> 00:28:17,569
lightning in the night, and half of it split away.
